 first-hand look at the detention center  which holds roughly 1500 mothers and  children about ten percent of them were  once separated but have been reunited I  think the reason this place was set up  is so that we could actually bring those  people through this island  and get a final decision on what their  case is like still legal advocates  working with these families say the  criteria for deciding who stays and who  gets deported is vague we are fighting  for them to all have their fair day in  court  now the Carmen and her daughter will be  heading back here to the facility in  Dili Texas it is expected that the judge  will start to speed up their case we  also reached out to the Department of  Justice and have yet to hear back from  them all right Maria thank you
 

